# Slide Typography — Fill the Frame

User has repeatedly complained: text too small, cards leave huge empty black padding. **Always prioritize large type that fills the row/card.**

## Hard rules

1. **Body / description text ≥ 20px** on content slides. Never ship 13–15px body copy in flex-stretched cards.
2. **Punch / headline lines inside cards ≥ 26–30px**. Card titles ≥ 28–32px.
3. **Section labels** (核心打法、维度名等) ≥ 16px, not 12–13px.
4. **If a card stretches with `flex-1`**, content must visually fill it: bump font size first; only then trim vertical padding (`py-2`–`py-3`, not `py-6`+). Do not leave a thin text band floating in a tall empty box.
5. **Prefer bigger type over more padding.** Empty space inside bordered cards is a bug, not “breathing room.”
6. Presentation canvas is roughly 16:9 full-bleed — design for distance reading, not dense dashboard UI.

## Anti-patterns

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — tiny copy in a tall flex row
<p className="text-[15px] text-zinc-400">{detail}</p>
<div className="text-[13px] text-zinc-500">核心打法</div>

// ✅ GOOD — type fills the card
<p className="text-[20px] text-zinc-300">{detail}</p>
<div className="text-[16px] text-zinc-500">核心打法</div>
<div className="text-[28px] font-black">{punch}</div>
```

When unsure, go **one step larger**, not smaller.
